{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Laver.</b> Like a large cauldron, and it has spouts that draw off water through their mouths." "<b>And its base.</b> As the Targum renders: its base — a prepared stand for the laver." "<b>For washing.</b> Refers to the laver." "<b>And between the altar.</b> The altar of burnt offering, for it is written of it that it is at the entrance of the tent of meeting, and the laver was drawn slightly inward and stood in the space between the altar and the tabernacle, and it did not intervene between them at all, because it is stated: ״וְאֵת מִזְבַּח הָעֹלָה שָׂם פֶּתַח מִשְׁכַּן אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד״ (Exodus 40) — meaning, the altar is at the entrance of the tent of meeting, but the laver is not at the entrance of the tent of meeting. How so? It was drawn slightly inward toward the south; so it is taught in Zevachim."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:47.817957902Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}